body:
Experiencing the same behaviour, styles are not in the DOM until the page is refreshed; working as expected in dev, not in build.

We have used a pattern of defining a loading variant of our components that utilise the same styles and so share a CSS module file, the loading.tsx imports the loading variant of the component, page.tsx imports the default variant. Where we `prefetch` on a `next/Link` to a page so that the loading.tsx is not required styles are applied as expected.

**--Update--**
Experimented with importing styles for the loading component from a different css module than the default component, this didn't resolve the issue for us.

However changing the path of the imported component from using a root-level index.ts to the component itself did (whilst still sharing styles through the same css module for the 2 variants).

## Broken

```js
// components/Pages/FilteredViewings/index.tsx
export * from "./FilteredViewings";
export * from "./FilteredViewingsLoading";
```

```js
// app/viewings/loading.tsx
import { FilteredViewingsLoading } from "@/components/Pages/FilteredViewings";
```

```js
// app/viewings/page.tsx
import { FilteredViewings } from "@/components/Pages/FilteredViewings";
```

## Working

```js
// app/viewings/loading.tsx
import { FilteredViewingsLoading } from "@/components/Pages/FilteredViewings/FilteredViewingsLoading";
```

```js
// app/viewings/page.tsx
import { FilteredViewings } from "@/components/Pages/FilteredViewings/FilteredViewings";
```

This issue exists in next v14.0.1 too!
tailwind css doesnt load in dynamic routes [app router]
@ztanner could you pls look into this issue!
